  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe Agricultural Growth Programme - Knowledge and Innovation Services (ZAGP KIS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contract is about the strengthening of the agricultural extension, research and education institutions in the framework of modernised farmer / value chain centric knowledge and innovation services. This will be done through two components: 1) the development and implementation of a new service and business model for market oriented and demand driven knowledge and innovation services around two institutions (TBC Gwebi college and Matopos research station) with direct strengthening of 4 district and 24 ward extension services (outcome 1)2) the strengthening of all research, education and extension to deliver as per the new model (outcome 2)</narrative>
  </description>
